E('mahatma gandhi|gandhi', 'Mahatma Gandhi was the leader of India’s non-violent independence movement against British rule.', 'He lived from 1869 to 1948.',
  'He trained as a lawyer in London and worked in South Africa for over twenty years.', 'He developed satyagraha, non-violent resistance.', 'His Salt March of 1930 protested a British tax on salt.', 'India won independence in 1947.', 'He was assassinated by a Hindu nationalist in January 1948.', '“Mahatma” is an honorific meaning “great soul”.',
  'He inspired civil rights movements worldwide, including Martin Luther King Jr.')
E('indian independence|partition of india|partition', 'India gained independence from Britain, and was partitioned into India and Pakistan.', 'Independence came on 15 August 1947.',
  'Partition split British India along mostly religious lines.', 'Around 15 million people were displaced.', 'Violence killed somewhere between several hundred thousand and two million people.', 'Jawaharlal Nehru became India’s first prime minister.', 'Muhammad Ali Jinnah founded Pakistan.',
  'Partition still shapes relations between India and Pakistan.')
E('martin luther king|martin luther king jr|mlk|i have a dream', 'Martin Luther King Jr. was an American Baptist minister and leader of the civil rights movement.', 'He lived from 1929 to 1968.',
  'He led the Montgomery bus boycott in 1955 and 1956.', 'He championed non-violent protest, inspired by Gandhi.', 'He gave his “I Have a Dream” speech at the March on Washington in August 1963.', 'He won the Nobel Peace Prize in 1964.', 'His work helped pass the Civil Rights Act of 1964 and the Voting Rights Act of 1965.', 'He was assassinated in Memphis on 4 April 1968.',
  'The US honours him with a national holiday each January.')
E('rosa parks', 'Rosa Parks was an American civil rights activist.', 'She lived from 1913 to 2005.',
  'On 1 December 1955 she refused to give up her bus seat to a white passenger in Montgomery, Alabama.', 'Her arrest sparked the Montgomery bus boycott.', 'The boycott lasted over a year and ended segregation on the city’s buses.', 'She had been an active member of the NAACP for years.',
  'She is called “the mother of the civil rights movement”.')
E('civil rights movement', 'The civil rights movement was a struggle to end racial segregation and discrimination against Black Americans.', 'It was at its height from the mid-1950s to the late 1960s.',
  'In 1954 the Supreme Court ruled school segregation unconstitutional in Brown v. Board of Education.', 'Protests included boycotts, sit-ins, freedom rides and marches.', 'Leaders included Martin Luther King Jr., Rosa Parks, John Lewis and Malcolm X.', 'The Civil Rights Act of 1964 banned discrimination.', 'The Voting Rights Act of 1965 protected voting rights.',
  'It transformed American law and inspired movements around the world.')
E('malcolm x', 'Malcolm X was an American Muslim minister and human rights activist.', 'He lived from 1925 to 1965.',
  'He was a powerful spokesman for the Nation of Islam.', 'He called for Black self-defence and pride.', 'After a pilgrimage to Mecca in 1964 he softened his views on race.', 'He was assassinated in February 1965.', 'The Autobiography of Malcolm X became a classic.',
  'He remains a major figure in the history of Black empowerment.')
E('nelson mandela|mandela|apartheid', 'Nelson Mandela was a South African anti-apartheid leader who became the country’s first Black president.', 'He lived from 1918 to 2013 and was president from 1994 to 1999.',
  'Apartheid was a system of racial segregation in South Africa from 1948 to the early 1990s.', 'Mandela was imprisoned for 27 years, much of it on Robben Island.', 'He was released in 1990.', 'He and President F. W. de Klerk shared the Nobel Peace Prize in 1993.', 'He promoted reconciliation rather than revenge.',
  'He is a global symbol of forgiveness and the fight for justice.')
E('john f kennedy|jfk|kennedy|kennedy assassination', 'John F. Kennedy was the 35th President of the United States.', 'He lived from 1917 to 1963 and was president from 1961.',
  'At 43 he was the youngest person elected president.', 'He faced the Cuban Missile Crisis in 1962.', 'He set the goal of landing a man on the Moon before the decade was out.', 'He was assassinated in Dallas on 22 November 1963.', 'Lee Harvey Oswald was charged, but was himself shot before trial.',
  'His death remains one of the most discussed events in American history.')
E('mao zedong|mao|chairman mao|cultural revolution', 'Mao Zedong was the founder of the People’s Republic of China and its leader until his death.', 'He lived from 1893 to 1976 and proclaimed the PRC in 1949.',
  'He led Communist forces in the Chinese Civil War.', 'The Long March of 1934 and 1935 made him a legend.', 'His Great Leap Forward caused a famine that killed tens of millions.', 'His Cultural Revolution from 1966 brought persecution and chaos.',
  'He remains a towering and controversial figure in China.')
E('ronald reagan|reagan', 'Ronald Reagan was the 40th US President, and formerly a Hollywood actor.', 'He lived from 1911 to 2004 and was president from 1981 to 1989.',
  'He cut taxes and championed free markets.', 'He survived an assassination attempt in 1981.', 'He negotiated arms reduction with Gorbachev.',
  'He is seen as one of the most influential modern conservatives.')
E('margaret thatcher|thatcher', 'Margaret Thatcher was the first female Prime Minister of the United Kingdom.', 'She lived from 1925 to 2013 and was PM from 1979 to 1990.',
  'She was nicknamed the “Iron Lady”.', 'She privatised many state industries and weakened trade unions.', 'She led Britain in the Falklands War in 1982.',
  'She remains one of Britain’s most admired and most divisive leaders.')
E('queen elizabeth ii|elizabeth ii|the queen', 'Elizabeth II was Queen of the United Kingdom and other Commonwealth realms.', 'She lived from 1926 to 2022 and reigned from 1952.',
  'She reigned for 70 years, the longest of any British monarch.', 'She served as a mechanic and driver in the Second World War.', 'Her coronation in 1953 was one of the first to be televised.', 'She was succeeded by her son, Charles III.',
  'She was a symbol of continuity through enormous change.')
E('barack obama|obama', 'Barack Obama was the 44th President of the United States and the first African American to hold the office.', 'He was born in 1961 and was president from 2009 to 2017.',
  'He was born in Hawaii.', 'He won the Nobel Peace Prize in 2009.', 'His Affordable Care Act expanded health insurance.', 'He led the US through the aftermath of the 2008 financial crisis.',
  'His election was a landmark in American history.')
E('che guevara|che', 'Che Guevara was an Argentine Marxist revolutionary.', 'He lived from 1928 to 1967.',
  'He trained as a doctor.', 'He was a key leader of the Cuban Revolution with Fidel Castro.', 'He was captured and executed in Bolivia in 1967.', 'A famous photograph of him became a worldwide icon.',
  'He is seen as a hero by some and a ruthless figure by others.')
E('fidel castro|castro|cuban revolution', 'Fidel Castro was the revolutionary leader of Cuba.', 'He lived from 1926 to 2016 and led Cuba from 1959 to 2008.',
  'His revolution overthrew the dictator Fulgencio Batista in 1959.', 'He made Cuba a one-party communist state allied with the USSR.', 'He survived many US assassination attempts.',
  'He is remembered as both a symbol of defiance and an authoritarian ruler.')
E('suffragettes|women’s suffrage|womens suffrage|emmeline pankhurst|votes for women', 'The suffragettes and suffragists campaigned for women’s right to vote.', 'The movement was strongest from the late 19th century to the 1920s.',
  'New Zealand was the first country to give women the vote, in 1893.', 'In Britain, Emmeline Pankhurst led the militant Women’s Social and Political Union.', 'British women over 30 won the vote in 1918, and on equal terms with men in 1928.', 'American women won the vote with the 19th Amendment in 1920.',
  'Their campaign transformed democracy.')
E('marie curie|curie', 'Marie Curie was a physicist and chemist who pioneered research on radioactivity.', 'She lived from 1867 to 1934.',
  'She was born in Poland and worked in France.', 'She discovered the elements polonium and radium with her husband, Pierre.', 'She was the first woman to win a Nobel Prize.', 'She is the only person to win Nobel Prizes in two different sciences: physics and chemistry.', 'Her notebooks are still too radioactive to handle without protection.', 'She died of a blood disorder probably caused by radiation exposure.',
  'She opened the door to women in science and to modern nuclear physics.')
E('albert einstein|einstein|relativity|e=mc2|theory of relativity', 'Albert Einstein was a German-born physicist, one of the greatest scientists of all time.', 'He lived from 1879 to 1955.',
  'In 1905 he published four groundbreaking papers.', 'His special relativity showed that time and space depend on how fast you move.', 'It produced the equation E = mc², linking mass and energy.', 'His general relativity of 1915 explained gravity as the bending of spacetime.', 'He won the 1921 Nobel Prize for explaining the photoelectric effect.', 'He fled Nazi Germany and settled in the United States in 1933.',
  'GPS satellites have to correct for relativity to work.')
